cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper."
title: "A fine-tuning headline inside its training-seed spread: a retraction, and the instrument that would have caught it"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Theodoro
    given-names: Caio
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7343-981X"
date-released: 2026-11-23
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/caiotheodoro/reconforge"
keywords:
  - negative results
  - retraction
  - random seeds
  - fine-tuning
  - pre-registration
  - LoRA
  - evaluation
abstract: >-
  A retraction. A 1.7B LoRA fine-tune was reported to beat a frontier model on
  severity-weighted recall by 0.0288; a pre-registered rule on the spread across
  training seeds fired against it. Code is Apache-2.0, the paper CC BY 4.0. Not
  peer reviewed.
